  "description": "issue #674 (SP2): `tell [ :a :b ]` addresses two turtles, so the single `forward 50` applies once per addressed turtle (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md's Per-turtle state: a turtle command applies once for each addressed turtle). Each turtle emits its own `move`+`draw-segment` pair carrying its `turtle_id` (1 then 2) — the events are stamped because the addressed set is now explicit (a `tell` has run), unlike the implicit main turtle whose events carry no `turtle_id`. Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
